SUMMARY:The Social Network (2010)
LOCATION:The Marquee\, Union South
DESCRIPTION:USA | 120 Min | PG-13 | Dir. David Fincher\n \nIn 2003\, Harv
 ard undergrad and computer genius Mark Zuckerberg (Jesse Eisenberg) begin
 s work on a new concept that eventually turns into the global social netw
 ork known as Facebook. Six years later\, he is one of the youngest billio
 naires ever\, but Zuckerberg finds that his unprecedented success leads t
 o both personal and legal complications when he ends up on the receiving 
 end of two lawsuits\, one involving his former friend (Andrew Garfield). 
 Based on the book "The Accidental Billionaires." - Rotten Tomatoes\n \nD
 avid Fincher's film has the rare quality of being not only as smart as it
 s brilliant hero\, but in the same way. It is cocksure\, impatient\, cold
 \, exciting and instinctively perceptive.-Roger Ebert of the Chicago Sun-
 Times\n \nWatch the trailer here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lB95KL
 mpLR4 \n\n \n\n \n \nFor information on available assistive content f
 or WUD Film screenings\, please visit the Assistive Movie Screenings in t
 he Marquee Theater page.  \nVisit our Informed Moviegoing Resources pag
 e for links to resources that explore film ratings and content alerts.\nT
 his event is intended for UW-Madison students\, faculty\, staff\, Wiscons
 in Union members and their guests. Anyone can become a Wisconsin Union me
 mber.\n\nhttps://union.wisc.edu/events-and-activities/event-calendar/even
 t/wud-film-presents-social-network-2010\n\nSource: WUD Film (The Marquee)
URL:https://union.wisc.edu/events-and-activities/event-calendar/event/wud-
 film-presents-social-network-2010
